        <p>
          Coursera completed its combination with Udemy on 11 May 2026. Udemy stopped trading, each Udemy share converted into 0.8 Coursera shares, and the combined company claims 315,000 courses and roughly 290 million registered learners. Coursera says nothing changes for learners for now: your Udemy courses, subscriptions and certificates stay where they are, and the two sites continue to operate separately. But the company has targeted $115 million in annual cost savings, and a marketplace that already relies on instructor goodwill is exactly where cost pressure tends to show up first. The sensible response is not panic; it is knowing where else you would go.
        </p>

        <h2 id="criteria">What to look for in a Udemy alternative</h2>
        <p>
